---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const P1 = `aList ← [8, 3, 9, 3, 5]
target ← 3
i ← 1
count ← 0

REPEAT UNTIL(i > LENGTH(aList))
{
  IF(aList[i] = target)
  {
    DISPLAY(i)
    count ← count + 1
  }
  i ← i + 1
}

DISPLAY(count)`;
const P2 = `aList ← [4, 11, 19, 26, 33, 41, 58, 70, 82]

PROCEDURE search(list, target)
{
  low ← 1
  high ← LENGTH(list)

  REPEAT UNTIL(low > high)
  {
    sum ← low + high
    mid ← (sum - (sum MOD 2)) / 2
    DISPLAY(mid)

    IF(list[mid] = target)
    {
      RETURN(mid)
    }
    IF(list[mid] < target)
    {
      low ← mid + 1
    }
    ELSE
    {
      high ← mid - 1
    }
  }
  RETURN(-1)
}

result ← search(aList, 58)
DISPLAY(result)`;
const P3 = `aList ← [4, 11, 19, 26, 33, 41, 58, 70, 82]

PROCEDURE search(list, target)
{
  low ← 1
  high ← LENGTH(list)

  REPEAT UNTIL(low > high)
  {
    sum ← low + high
    mid ← (sum - (sum MOD 2)) / 2
    DISPLAY(mid)

    IF(list[mid] = target)
    {
      RETURN(mid)
    }
    IF(list[mid] < target)
    {
      low ← mid + 1
    }
    ELSE
    {
      high ← mid - 1
    }
  }
  RETURN(-1)
}

result ← search(aList, 30)
DISPLAY(result)`;
const RefCard = `a ← expression            assign a COPY of the result to a
DISPLAY(expression)      show it, FOLLOWED BY A SPACE
=  ≠  >  <  ≥  ≤            comparison.  = means EQUALS

aList[1]                 THE FIRST ELEMENT. Not aList[0]
LENGTH(aList)            how many elements

a MOD b                  remainder.  17 MOD 5 is 2
a / b                    TRUE division.  17 / 5 is 3.4
                         there is no rounding operator on the sheet

REPEAT UNTIL(condition)  repeats UNTIL it becomes true
                         the INVERSE of a while loop

IF(condition) { } ELSE { }     the only two selection forms`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Pseudocode Challenge: Tracing a Search</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            Three searches in exam notation. <b>Two of them are binary searches,
            which is a recurring exam pattern</b> &mdash; you are given a list
            and a target and asked what happens, with no computer in the room.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Watch the indexing.</b> Every list on this page starts at 1. The
            same search in JavaScript would return a number one lower.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Do this on paper.</b> There is nothing to run. On exam day you
            get this notation printed and no computer.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="reference">
          <h2>Reference Card</h2>

          <Code code={RefCard} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Exam Notation — what you have so far" showLineNumbers={false} class="mt-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="problems">
          <h2>The Problems</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 1 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>What does this display? Write down every character, including the spaces.</p>

          <Code code={P1} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 1" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Then answer this:</b> <code>DISPLAY</code> puts a space after
            every value. Write out the exact output string, and say how many
            characters long it is.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 2 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>
            Build a table with a row per pass: <code>low</code>,{" "}
            <code>high</code>, <code>mid</code>, and the value at{" "}
            <code>aList[mid]</code>. Then say what is displayed and what is
            returned.
          </p>

          <Code code={P2} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 2" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Then answer this:</b> the list has nine items and this search
            touched very few of them. How many comparisons did it make, and what
            is the most it could ever make on a list of nine?
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Problem 3 &mdash; trace</h3>

          <p>
            Same procedure, and <b>30 is not in the list</b>. Build the table
            again. What is displayed, and what is returned?
          </p>

          <Code code={P3} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Problem 3" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Then answer this:</b> the loop ended because{" "}
            <code>low</code> passed <code>high</code>. Write down the values they
            held on that last pass, and explain what it means for the range
            between them to be empty.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>And this:</b> <code>mid</code> is written as{" "}
            <code>(sum - (sum MOD 2)) / 2</code> rather than{" "}
            <code>(low + high) / 2</code>. Give an example where the second one
            produces something that is not a valid index.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your three answers, plus the trace tables for Problems 2 and 3.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>3 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
